"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">>"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kedgeconnectedsubgraphs(_:)"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kComponents()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"type":"topic","title":"kComponents()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kEdgeConnectedComponen